and it was the liberality of British institutions that saved Britain from revolution. But on the Ionian Islands, we don't see too much liberality. What we see is a lot of flogging and hanging. And in fact, there's a, you know, there's a kind of Europe-wide scandal over how the British handled this uprising in Kefalonia. And so that's an interesting example of, you know, when you actually do see British authorities facing a local tumult of the kind that broke out across the continent. We don't see that they behave more or less as the Austrians and the Prussians and other European states do.
正是英国制度的自由度拯救了英国免于革命。但在爱奥尼亚群岛，我们并没有看到太多的自由。我们看到的是大量的鞭笞和绞刑。事实上，这是一个——你知道的——欧洲范围内关于英国人如何处理凯法利尼亚这场起义的丑闻。所以这是一个有趣的例子，当你真正看到英国当局面临蔓延到整个欧洲大陆的那种本土动乱时。我们看到他们的行为或多或少与奥地利人、普鲁士人和其他欧洲国家一样。

