73
00:44:43.000 --> 00:45:02.000
It rained very heavily, didn't it? I hope so. The rain very heavily, didn't it? The rain stopped play, basically. Which is never a help. But in addition, 80,000 special constables turned up. Including Gladstone. Exactly. And including the future Napoleon III, who'd signed up as a special constable, was hoping to get his hands on some chartists and give them a right drubbing.
雨下得很大，对吧？希望如此。雨下得很大，对吧？雨水基本上制止了游行。这从来没什么帮助。但此外，8万名特别警察出现了。包括格莱斯顿。没错。包括后来成为拿破仑三世的人，他报名当了特别警察，希望能抓到一些宪章派并好好教训他们一顿。

74
00:45:02.000 --> 00:45:31.000
Never got the chance to do that. You know, but there's a commentary by a Tory at the time called Sibthorpe, a sort of ultra-Tory, who says that, you know, by gum, if only those special constables had a chance to get stuck into those chartists, they would have given them such a hiding as no man ever received. And I think he wasn't wrong. I mean, what's special about Britain is it could mobilize, out of its own society, counter-revolutionary forces on a scale which we don't see anywhere else in Europe.
从来没有机会那样做。你知道的，当时有个叫西布索普的保守党人做过评论，那是个极端保守党人，他说，天哪，要是那些特别警察有机会跟那些宪章派大干一场的话，他们会给他们一顿这辈子从没挨过的狠揍。我认为他说得没毛病。我的意思是，英国的特别之处在于，它能从自身的社会中动员起在欧洲其他任何地方都看不到规模的反革命力量。

75
00:45:31.000 --> 00:45:48.000
You know, Giselle can't summon up 80,000 special constables wielding clubs. Because these people are volunteers, right? Yeah. These people are volunteers. Exactly. They're not even paid. They want to get stuck in. Yeah. They're not even paid. They want to get stuck in. So there's a sense in which you have a sufficiently large
你知道的，吉赛尔可召唤不出8万名挥舞着俱乐部的特别警察。因为这些人都是志愿者，对吧？是的。这些人都是志愿者。没错。他们甚至没有薪水。他们就是想加入进来。对。他们甚至没有薪水。他们就是想大干一场。所以某种意义上说，你拥有一个足够庞大的

