of the great sort of discoveries for the conservatives that, you know, perhaps it's us. This is what they're saying. Anyway, perhaps we're the ones who really know the little people. Yeah. The revolutions were living in a bubble, in an urban bubble. People like each other. So this is your 1968 parallel, right? That 1968 ends with the election of Richard Nixon and the war in Vietnam continues and all these kinds of things.
你知道的，也许是我们。他们是这么说的。不管怎样，也许我们才是真正了解底层民众的人。是的。革命者生活在泡沫中，生活在城市泡沫中。人们彼此喜欢。所以这就是你的1968年的平行事件，对吧？1968年以理查德·尼克松的当选而告终，越南战争仍在继续，诸如此类的事情。

