the person that he became because it was the revolution that allowed him to enter public life. And because it unleashes the power of nationalism, right? Because it creates the idea of the nation as the main vehicle for kind of popular idealism and aspirations and crowds and modernity. Nationalism is modern after 1848, isn't it? Well, that's right. Although Bismarck sees very clearly that nationalism is going to have to be a managed force. It'll have to be managed by a media which is itself carefully managed and overseen. And that's the great lesson of 1848, that nationalism kind of as a free-floating potential in European society is not going to achieve very much. But nationalism, when it's yoked to state power, will achieve enormous amounts. And that's what happens after 1848.
他后来那个人，因为正是革命允许他进入公共生活。并且因为它释放了民族主义的力量，对吧？因为它将民族创造为大众理想主义、追求、民众和现代性的主要载体。民族主义在1848年之后才变得现代，不是吗？嗯，是的。尽管俾斯麦非常清楚地看到民族主义将不得不成为一种被管控的力量。它必须由一个本身受到仔细管理和监督的媒体来管理。这就是1848年的伟大教训，民族主义作为欧洲社会中一种自由浮动的潜力，是不会取得太大成就的。但是民族主义，当它与国家权力结合在一起时，将取得巨大的成就。这就是1848年之后发生的事情。

