00:50:44.000 --> 00:51:19.000
So lots of the kind of the more radical constitutions and so on get repealed. And to that extent, we could perhaps talk of the ambitions and hopes of the more radical revolutionaries failing. But one of the things that struck me in the book was that actually, there are a number of constitutions in Europe that are still kind of basically current today that do reach back to 1848. So you mentioned Switzerland, I suppose, reached back to 1847, but the Netherlands. And I thought the most interesting one was Denmark, which had been the kind of absolute monarchy and then becomes a kind of model liberal democracy. And that constitution stays in place after 1848.
所以许多更激进的宪法等都被废除了。从这个程度上讲，我们或许可以说更激进革命者的雄心和希望失败了。但书中让我印象深刻的一点是，事实上，欧洲有许多宪法直到今天基本上仍然有效，它们确实可以追溯到1848年。所以你提到了瑞士，我想可以追溯到1847年，还有荷兰。我认为最有趣的是丹麦，它曾是某种专制君主制，然后变成了一种民主自由主义的模范。而那部宪法在1848年后一直保留了下来。

85
00:51:19.000 --> 00:52:09.000
Absolutely. To this day, the Danes still celebrate the day of the promulgation of that constitution, the June Basic Law. So it's, you know, that's just one of many examples of constitutions that still survive today. I mean, the Swiss Constitution of 1848, it's not until 1848 they actually promulgate it, is still in force with many amendments and so on. The Dutch Constitution of 18, the revised Dutch Constitution of 1849, which comes about as a result of the 1848 revolutions, those revisions are still in place. And, you know, in many ways, these, the Italians too, the Italian constitution winds up being the Piedmontese constitution. The Piedmontese constitution is issued in March 1848, the Statuto Albertino, and it too survives and bits of its language are still present in today's Italian constitution. And so are bits of the German constitution of 1848. They're still present in the Grundgesetz
绝对是的。直到今天，丹麦人仍在庆祝该宪法颁布的日子，即六月基本法。所以，你知道，这只是今天仍然存在的众多宪法中的一个例子。我的意思是，1848年的瑞士宪法——直到1848年他们才真正颁布它——在经过许多修正案等之后仍然有效。1848年革命带来的荷兰18世纪——修订后的1849年荷兰宪法，这些修订至今仍然有效。而且，你知道，在许多方面，这些——意大利也是如此，意大利宪法最终变成了皮埃蒙特宪法。皮埃蒙特宪法于1848年3月颁布，即《阿尔贝托法典》（Statuto Albertino），它也幸存下来，其语言的碎片仍然存在于今天的意大利宪法中。1848年德国宪法的碎片也是如此。它们仍然存在于今天的德意志联邦共和国基本法中。因此，在这些革命过程中取得的巨大成果确实经受住了时间的考验并得以幸存。我们真的没有时间去探讨它，但你也认为现代当代天主教也可以追溯到这个时期。那也是一个迷人的故事。天主教教会——我们没有时间讲那个了，但它必须彻底重塑自己。它确实在1848年之后做到了这一点。而我们认为是天主教教会的大部分内容，实际上正是诞生于那个时刻。你最后的台词是，你基本上说，当我们回顾过去时，我们不应该看到我们自己。我的意思是，我想你基本上是说，

86
00:52:09.000 --> 00:52:45.000
of today's German Federal Republic. So a huge amount of what was achieved in the course of these revolutions did stand the test of time and did survive. We haven't really got time to touch it, but you also argue that modern contemporary Catholicism dates back to this time as well. That's another fascinating story. The Catholic Church, we don't have time for that, but it has to completely remake itself. And it does in the aftermath of 1848. And most of what we think of as the Catholic Church is actually born in that moment. And your last lines, so you basically say, we're not supposed to see ourselves when we look back in the past. I mean, I think so you basically say, we're not supposed to see ourselves
当我们回顾过去时，我们不应该看到我们自己。我的意思是，我想汤姆和我完全同意这一点。然而，有趣的是，你认为1848年的革命者能在我们身上看到他们自己。所以你发现当时与现在的共鸣非常惊人。我发现它们非常惊人。我想在那个结束评语中表达两点。一是，你知道，共鸣是存在的。你越是去思考它们，它们就越多，也越显得有说服力。第二点是，那些过去的人很聪明。我们很容易把过去的人看作是带着有缺陷的计划等的怪人，尤其是当他们的计划没有实现时。

87
